# bashbasicsbyvk_tidy.list — which TEMPLATE every menu is built on (🧶 tidy prints it).   template ID | template | key | file
# The ID is the file: templates/bashbasicsbyvk_<ID>.sh.tpl lays the screen out; bashbasicsbyvk_tpl_defs.sh defines every {placeholder} once;
# bashbasicsbyvk_tpl.sh is the processor.  Screens on the same template share the ID.  key: fn:<function that draws the screen> or map:<command map>.
# The innermost listed function on the call stack wins, then the map.  Change a screen with  bashbasicsbyvk_tidy_gen --set KEY TEMPLATE.
